00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:57.400
He uses middleman

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.400
That is your API

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.400
And server doesn't directly

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.400
Responds back to client

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.400
He also uses APIs

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.400
And what is the benefit of this

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.400
The benefit is

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.400
Your application

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.400
Which you call your backend

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.400
You can develop it separately

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.400
And your client side

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.400
Frontend

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.400
Through which you interact with your application

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:23.400
You can develop it separately

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.400
Here you

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.400
Break their interlinkage

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.400
They are not dependent on each other

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.400
And that is the power of API

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.400
If I

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.400
Tell you about your LLM based applications

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.400
Specifically

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.400
APIs are basically used

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.400
To serve your application

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.400
If someone asks you in an interview

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.400
Why are you

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.400
Implementing APIs in your application

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:49.400
What is the reason behind it

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.400
You simply have to say

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.400
We are using APIs here because

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.400
We have to serve this application

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.400
To our client or to our user

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.400
Till now what we were doing

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.400
We were directly

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.400
Loading our application

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.400
You know we were importing

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.400
In the code

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.400
And using our application

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.400
Which is not a good idea

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.400
The problem is

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.400
When your backend and frontend

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.400
Are so tightly coupled

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.400
If in your backend code

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.400
There is a slight change

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.400
You have to change your frontend

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.400
Which is not a good thing

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.400
Frontend developers are different

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.400
And the application you are making

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.400
You as an AI engineer

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.400
Are a separate developer

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.400
So you have to decouple both

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.400
You have to remove the coupling

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.400
Then we discussed further

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.400
That your API frameworks

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.400
Were coming in Python

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.400
That is Flask

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.400
And Django

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:49.400
These are actually very good frameworks

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.400
These are basically your mature frameworks

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.400
They are being used in the industry for many years

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.400
But

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.400
Their biggest problem is

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.400
That they handle your API calls

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.400
In a synchronous way

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.400
They handle your requests one by one

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:05.400
Till your one request

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.400
Is not processed completely

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.400
They don't take the other request

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.400
So here we need to

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.400
Use a framework

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.400
Where we can take asynchronous

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.400
Responses

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.400
What will be the main benefit of this

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.400
You will get

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.400
While you are scaling your application

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.400
Your one application

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.400
Is deployed at one place

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.400
Let's say on AWS

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.400
And multiple users

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:33.400
Interact with that application

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.400
At a single time

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.400
Your application is having

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.400
Let's say a thousand users

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.400
So thousand users can use

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.400
Your application concurrently

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.400
That's why we use asynchronous

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.400
APIs

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.400
And here in the picture

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.400
Fast API

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.400
Fast API's core philosophy

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.400
Is your asynchronous philosophy

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.400
You can understand it like this

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.400
Fast API is built on

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.400
Some core primitives

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.400
First of all

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.400
Starlet

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.400
Starlet is your web framework

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.400
We discussed

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:13.400
How do APIs communicate

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.400
Through the HTTP protocol

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.400
So they communicate

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:19.400
On the web or internet

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.400
And who handles that communication

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.400
Starlet

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.400
Starlet is an asynchronous

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.400
Framework

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.400
Starlet uses

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.400
A particular component

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:33.400
Which is called

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.400
ASGI

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.400
Which is your asynchronous gateway interface

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.400
So this is asynchronous

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.400
What is its function

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.400
It acts as a translator

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.400
It acts as a translator

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:47.400
It translates your HTTP request

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.400
Into python

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.400
It translates it into python understandable code

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.400
It translates it

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.400
Third is your server

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.400
Which basically

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.400
Is used to deploy

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.400
Or run

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.400
And you are using that too

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.400
Uvcon

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.400
The server you get in Flask or Django

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.400
Is G-Unicon

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:11.400
That is a synchronous web server

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.400
The web server you use here

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.400
Uvcon that is also asynchronous in nature

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.400
I hope you remember this

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.400
And we also discussed

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.400
In detail that what is the difference between

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.400
Parallelism and concurrency

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.400
So fast API doesn't give you parallelism

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.400
It gives you concurrency

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.400
I hope all these points are clear to you

